# Use Named Function Declarations for Package-Level Helpers

Prefer `func` declarations over `var`-assigned function literals for package-level helper functions.

```go
// ❌ BAD
var buildTapePath = func(id string) string {
    return "output/" + id + ".tape"
}

// ✅ GOOD
func buildTapePath(id string) string {
    return "output/" + id + ".tape"
}
```

Named `func` declarations are idiomatic Go, show up in stack traces with their real name, are callable before their declaration in the file, and communicate intent more clearly than a `var` holding an anonymous function.

This does not apply to closures passed as arguments, returned from functions, or registered as Gin handlers inline.
